    <p>Every time a browser shows a padlock icon, a chain of trust is working behind the scenes. Public Key Infrastructure, or PKI, is the system of certificate authorities, certificates, and revocation checks that makes it possible to know a server, a device, or a person really is who they claim to be. It underpins HTTPS, code signing, VPN authentication, and encrypted email.</p>

    <p>By the end of this room you will understand how root, intermediate, and issuing certificate authorities work together, how certificates are issued and eventually revoked, and how a poorly managed PKI can quietly open the door to impersonation and man in the middle attacks. A hands-on practical is included so you can apply these ideas directly.</p>

