// TASK 3: Certificate Templates & Auto-Enrolment
$task_contents[3] = <<<'HTML'
<div class="content-block">
    <h2>Standardizing How Certificates Get Issued</h2>

    <p>Issuing thousands of certificates by hand is not realistic in any organization of scale. A certificate template defines the policy for a class of certificates in advance: what key usage it allows, how long it is valid, and what naming rules it must follow. Think of a template as a blueprint or a preformatted form that every certificate of that type must match.</p>

    <p>Auto-enrolment builds on top of templates. It automatically requests and issues certificates to devices or users that meet a template's criteria, without a human approving each one individually. This makes large scale deployments practical, but the template still enforces the policy boundaries, auto-enrolment does not mean unrestricted issuance.</p>

