// TASK 6: PKI Failures & Impersonation/MITM Risk
$task_contents[6] = <<<'HTML'
<div class="content-block">
    <h2>When PKI Engineering Goes Wrong</h2>

    <p>PKI is only as strong as its weakest configuration decision. Three mistakes appear again and again in real deployments: keys that are too short to resist modern cracking, validity periods that stay far too long, and certificates issued without any revocation checking configured at all. None of these mistakes are exotic, they are simply careless defaults left unexamined.</p>

    <p>On their own, each mistake is a weakness. Combined, they create a direct path to impersonation and man in the middle attacks. A weak key can be forged, a long validity period gives an attacker more time to use a stolen or forged certificate, and missing revocation checking means nobody catches it even after the certificate is reported compromised.</p>

    <h3>Failure to Consequence</h3>
    <table class="content-table">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Failure</th>
                <th>Consequence</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td>Weak key length</td>
                <td>Signatures can potentially be forged, undermining the certificate's identity guarantee</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Excessive validity period</td>
                <td>Extends the window an attacker can exploit a compromised certificate</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>No revocation checking</td>
                <td>Stolen or revoked certificates continue to be trusted by relying parties</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <!-- SVG: MITM via missing revocation check
         Teaching purpose: show concretely how a policy failure becomes an active attack,
         which they would otherwise see as three unrelated checklist items. -->
    <div style="margin: 20px 0;">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 700 160" width="100%" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="MITM attack enabled by missing revocation checking">
            <rect x="10"  y="55" width="140" height="50" rx="8" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--border)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <text x="80" y="85" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="600" fill="var(--text-primary)">Client</text>
