            <rect x="550" y="55" width="140" height="50" rx="8" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--border)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <text x="620" y="85" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="600" fill="var(--text-primary)">Real Server</text>
            <line x1="150" y1="80" x2="275" y2="55" stroke="var(--text-secondary)" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#arr6)"/>
            <line x1="440" y1="55" x2="545" y2="80" stroke="var(--text-secondary)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="4 3"/>
            <defs>
                <marker id="arr6" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="6" refY="3" orient="auto">
                    <path d="M0,0 L0,6 L8,3 z" fill="var(--text-secondary)"/>
                </marker>
            </defs>
        </svg>
    </div>

    <div class="warning-box">
        <h4><i class="fas fa-exclamation-triangle"></i> Compounding Risk</h4>
        <p>These three failures rarely appear in isolation. A PKI audit should always check key length, validity period, and revocation configuration together, since any one of them left unchecked can undermine the other two.</p>
    </div>
</div>
